# Canonical identity mapping for contributors (git built-in, see `git help mailmap`).
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email>  Commit Name <commit@email>
#         left = canonical (displayed), right = original signature in history
#
# Why this file exists: of the 13 signature identities in this repo, only 7 can be
# resolved to a GitHub login via the `users.noreply.github.com` email format. The rest
# use real addresses (gmail / 163 / outlook), so the account name cannot be derived
# from the data -- it needs one manual confirmation, recorded here once.
# scripts/gen-contributors.mjs depends on this to work reliably.
#
# Side benefit: `git shortlog -sne` also merges the multiple identities of one person.
#
# NOTE: keep comments ASCII-only. Verified: non-ASCII comment lines break mailmap
# parsing for the lines that follow them (git 2.56).

# Maintainer: "Black Cat" / "Xynrin" are two display names of one person, three emails.
Black Cat <203426472+yxxbc@users.noreply.github.com>  Black Cat <203426472+Francis-Xavier-code@users.noreply.github.com>
Black Cat <203426472+yxxbc@users.noreply.github.com>  Black Cat <xynrin@outlook.com>
Black Cat <203426472+yxxbc@users.noreply.github.com>  Xynrin <xynrin@outlook.com>

# Upstream author: two display names plus one real address.
cshuangyy <121596361+cshuangyy@users.noreply.github.com>  cshuangyy <mycitu@163.com>
cshuangyy <121596361+cshuangyy@users.noreply.github.com>  Zhouzhou <121596361+cshuangyy@users.noreply.github.com>

